{
 "about": "The (style, slot) pairs whose tdl_resolve_kit and /api/kit answer moved when WP-14.26 rebased core.resolve_kit on build/resolve_kit.resolve_slots. Measured on 25 Sep 2026 by comparing every slot of every style, resolve_kit(style, slot=slot, only_specified=False), on a git archive of 5aa8041 (hand_merge) against this tree (resolved). `pairs` differ on the binding, the canonical set or the forbidden set; `rule_moves` are rows both readings bind whose rule text differs. The before column is a record of what was served and is never re-derived by a test: the hand-merge that produced it is deleted.",
 "causes": {
  "open-stops": "the hand-merge stopped at an `open` record carrying a status and served it (the node that wrote `open` as the source); resolve_slots treats `open` as transparent and walks on to the ancestor that settles the slot (OQ 87's mechanism)",
  "scope": "the style reaches an ancestor through a scoped edge (OQ 58, `_cascade_scope`) that does not carry this slot; the hand-merge ignored the scope",
  "extends-restates-rule": "an `extends` delta restates the slot's `rule`; the hand-merge merged parameters, variants and five named fields and never `rule`, so it served the ancestor's sentence under the child's provenance",
  "replace-on-a-duplicate-id": "the base slot lists one variant id twice (a permitted record and a conditional canonical one); an `op: replace` delta matched the FIRST copy in the hand-merge and the LAST in apply_variant_ops, so the hand-merge served the variant as canonical and forbidden at once",
  "rule-append-join": "`rule_append` joined with \". \" by the hand-merge and with \" \" by merge_extends; the words are the same"
 },
 "total_pairs_compared": 15908,
